  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.1.0-preview.5 - The robot's camera as pictures (RoseAudioLink.OnVideoFrame, H.264 decoded by SpawnDev.RTC) and as a track for browser hosts (OnVideoTrack); paced live speech to the robot over WebRTC (RobotSpeechStreamer) and clip upload/play over the robot's data channel (RobotDataChannel, FLAC, about 7x faster with SctpMaxBurst 32); ReachyBody facing (TurnTowardAsync, persistent facing); ParkAsync turns the motors off only after the sleep move has finished. On SpawnDev.RTC 2.4.0. 0.1.0-preview.4 - Dependency update, no Reachy code change: SpawnDev.RTC 2.2.3 -> 2.3.1, the SpawnDev.SpawnJS 3 line (with SpawnDev.MultiMedia 2.4, SpawnDev.SpawnJS.Cryptography 2.1 and SpawnDev.SIPSorcery 10.0.10, which handles SCTP FORWARD TSN so a desktop data channel survives a peer that abandons unreliable chunks). Before this, an app on SpawnJS 3 that referenced Reachy resolved RTC 2.2.3 and its SpawnJS 2 dependency set. Full history: CHANGELOG.md",
